---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import ArticleOffer from '../components/ArticleOffer.astro';
import { pg14Facts as f } from '../data/facts';

const title = 'PostgreSQL 14 End of Life: What Changes on 12 November 2026';
const description = 'PostgreSQL 14 gets its final community release on 12 November 2026. What stops, what keeps running, the RDS, Aurora and Azure dates that follow, a tested inventory script, and how to choose a target version.';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'When does PostgreSQL 14 reach end of life?',
    a: `The PostgreSQL Global Development Group lists ${f.communityEol} as the final release date for PostgreSQL 14. After that release there are no more community bug or security fixes for the 14 branch. Managed services have later dates: AWS RDS and Aurora end standard support on ${f.rdsStandardSupportEnd}, and Azure Database for PostgreSQL Flexible Server on ${f.azureStandardSupportEnd}.`
  },
  {
    q: 'Will PostgreSQL 14 stop working after end of life?',
    a: 'No. Existing servers keep running and accepting connections. End of life means the community stops publishing fixes. Any security issue or data-corruption bug found later and fixed in 15 to 18 is not fixed in 14 by the community.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to RDS and Aurora PostgreSQL 14 instances?',
    a: `Nothing changes on ${f.communityEol}. Standard support continues until ${f.rdsStandardSupportEnd}. From ${f.rdsExtendedSupportYear1Start}, instances still on 14 with Extended Support enabled (the default) are enrolled in paid RDS Extended Support, billed per vCPU-hour, until ${f.rdsExtendedSupportEnd}. Some minor versions reach end of standard support earlier.`
  },
  {
    q: 'Which version should I upgrade PostgreSQL 14 to?',
    a: 'For most teams, PostgreSQL 17 or 18. PostgreSQL 18 has support until November 2030 and PostgreSQL 17 until November 2029. Pick the newest version that your platform, extensions, drivers, CDC tooling and ORM all support, then test it against a workload baseline.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I upgrade directly from PostgreSQL 14 to 18?',
    a: 'Yes. pg_upgrade and logical replication both support skipping major versions. On RDS and Aurora, check the valid upgrade targets for your exact minor version with aws rds describe-db-engine-versions, because the allowed targets depend on the source minor.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Is paying for RDS Extended Support a reasonable option?',
    a: 'It can be a deliberate bridge when something specific blocks the upgrade, such as a vendor application, a CDC pipeline that needs rework, or a planned platform move. It is an expensive default when the only blocker is scheduling.'
  }
];
---
<ArticleLayout
