  description={description}
  eyebrow="PostgreSQL upgrades · End of life"
  published="2026-10-13"
  updated="2026-11-11"
  offer="upgrade"
  schemaType="Article"
  faq={faq}
  ctaTitle="Still running PostgreSQL 14 in production?"
  ctaDescription="Send your platform, current minor version and extension list. A readiness review ranks the blockers per cluster, captures a performance baseline and gives you a dated, reversible upgrade plan."
>
  <p class="notice"><strong>Short answer:</strong> PostgreSQL 14 receives its final community release on <strong>{f.communityEol}</strong>. Your servers will not stop, but no further bug or security fixes will be published for the 14 branch. On AWS RDS and Aurora, standard support runs until <strong>{f.rdsStandardSupportEnd}</strong> and paid Extended Support starts on {f.rdsExtendedSupportYear1Start}. On Azure Flexible Server, standard support ends on {f.azureStandardSupportEnd}. Move to the final 14 minor release now, and plan the major upgrade from an inventory and a workload baseline rather than from the calendar.</p>

